<p>That's actually a good question. The tone of the story suggests that it should be contemplated as &quot;art&quot; but once you start panicking and thinking, &quot;jesus god this paint's trying to kill me!&quot; it doesn't stop, so as long as you were just thinking about it as a mess, graffiti, anything where you had to consciously consider it, it would trigger the effect. I think this holds since some art, particularly things like graffiti and similar vandalism, can be seen as challenging, intentionally offensive, counter-culture, etc., designed to cause reactions more than just art criticism.</p>

